lv török kapcsolatai a honfoglalás előtt és az Árpád-korban. Budapest:\\r\", \"Akadémiai Kiadó, 1986. 602 p.\\r\", \"23. Martin J. Treasure of the Land of Darkness. The fur trade and its signifi cance for medieval Russia.\\r\", \"Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1986. 296 p.\\r\", \"24. Martinez A. P. Gardīzī’s two Chapters on the Turks // AEMAe. Vol. 11 — 19. II2. 1982.\\r\", \"P. 109 — 218.\\r\", \"25. Miller D. B. Legends of the Icon of Our Lady of Vladimir: A Study of the Development of\\r\", \"Muscovite National Consciousness // Speculum XLIII. № 4. 1968. P. 657 — 670.\\r\", \"26. Minorsky V. Ḥudūd al-ʿĀlam. ’The Regions of the World.’ A Persian Geography 372 A.H. 982\\r\", \"A.D. GMS XI. London: Messrs, Luzak & Co, 1937. 544 p.\\r\", \"27. Minorsky V. Sharaf al-Zamān Tāhir Marvazī on China, the Turks and India. London: The Royal\\r\", \"Asiatic Society, 1942. 234 p.\\r\", \"28. Noonan T. S. Why dirhams fi rst reached Russia: the role of Arab— Khazar relations in the\\r\", \"development of the earliest Islamic trade with Eastern Europe: AEMAe. Vol. 4. 1984. P. 151 — 282.\\r\", \"29. Pelenski J. Russia and Kazan. Conquest and Imperial Ideology (1438 — 1560). The Hague, Paris:\\r\", \"Mouton, 1974. 349 p.\\r\", \"30. Rispling G. («The Volga Bulgarian Imitative Coinage of al-Amir Yaltawar (‘Barman’) and\\r\", \"Mikail b. Jafar», p. 275 — 282) traite des imitations, qui constituent 5 à 10 % du total des monnaies //\\r\", \"Commentationes de Nummis Saeculorum IX — XI. Sigtuna Papers. Proceedings of the Sigtuna Symposium\\r\", \"on Viking-Age Coinage 1 — 4 June 1989. Ed. K. Jonsson and B. Malmer. London, 1990. 339 p.\\r\", \"31. Scriptores Rerum Hungaricarum tempore ducum regumque stirpis Arpadianae gestarum. Edendo\\r\", \"operi praefuit Emericus Szentpétery. Vol. I. Budapest: Magyar Történelmi Társulat, 1937. № 4. 681 p.\\r\", \"32. Togan Z. V. Ibn Fadlān’s Reisebericht. Leipzig: Deutschen Morgenländischen Gesellschaft, 1939.\\r\", \"371 s.\\r\", \"33. Viae et regna, descriptio ditionis moslemicae auctore Abu’l-Kasim Ibn Haukal by Ibn Haukal,\\r\", \"Abu’l-Ksim, Muhammad; Goeje, M. J. de (Michael Jan). Vol. II. Lugdunum Batavorum: Brill, 1873. 436 p.\\r\", \"34. Viae Regnorum. Descriptio ditionis moslemicae auctore Abu Ishák al-Fárisí al-Istahrí. //\\r\", \"Bibliotheca Geographorum Arabicorum Vol. I. Ed. M. J. de Goeje. Lugduni Batavorum, 1870. 394 p.\\r\", \"35. Wyngaert A. Sinica Franciscana. Itinera et Relationes Fratrum Minorum saeculi XIII. et XIV.\\r\", \"B. 1. Quaracchi — Firenze: Apud Collegium S. Bonaventurae, 1929. CXVIII — 637 p.\\r\", \"36. Zimonyi I. Origins of the Volga Bulghars. Studia Uralo-Altaica 32. Szeged, 1990. 211 p.\"]', '[]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
